WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.040
We've talked before about the problem that
we have in political discourse.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.910
When one side doesn't accept facts, it is
a real impediment to being able to make progress

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.410
and have good faith debate about any issue
that we find important.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:20.240
And we're seeing that now front and center
with the Ukraine fiasco where only 40% of

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.780
Republicans, 40% of Republicans believe that
Donald Trump spoke to the Ukrainian president

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.539
about Joe Biden on the phone.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:32.119
Remember Donald Trump has admitted to this
that bogus transcript, which was actually

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:38.530
a memo, sort of a truncated summary of the
call, includes a discussion of Joe Biden between

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.170
Donald Trump and the Ukrainian president,
Ukrainian president.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:44.650
So let's take a step back and think about
opinion versus fact.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:50.270
If you pull people about something like their
opinion on gay marriage, it is far more reasonable

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:55.000
that you would have very different perspectives
from Democrats, Republicans, and now for me,

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.050
I think that the opinion on gay marriage,
there's only one right opinion on gay marriage,

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.960
but okay, this is a matter of opinion and
you would expect more difference in people's

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.780
opinion on gay marriage.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:11.409
But when Monmouth university polling Institute
asked people, do you believe that Donald Trump

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:14.720
spoke about Joe Biden on that phone call with
a Ukrainian president?

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.909
Almost all Democrats believed that that is
something that was discussed.

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:22.859
About 60% of independence believed that it
was something that was discussed, but only

00:01:22.859 --> 00:01:26.049
40% of Republicans believed it.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:30.009
Donald Trump admitted that they discussed
this on the call.

00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:33.679
Not only did Trump admit it when asked, but
the truncated transcript or memo that the

00:01:33.679 --> 00:01:37.759
white house released also includes the mention
of Biden.

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:39.109
So what do we do?

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:45.700
What do we do when one side won't even accept
inconvenient but verified facts that their

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.299
own leader gives to them?

00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:52.469
Now, of course, there's the separate question
of whether Donald Trump extorted or tried

00:01:52.469 --> 00:01:54.139
to extort Ukraine.

00:01:54.139 --> 00:01:58.939
And there's lots of other questions, but Trump
admitted that they spoke about Biden and 60%

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:01.720
of Republicans either don't believe it or
don't know.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.249
Now there are some possible questions about
this poll.

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:09.640
It was conducted during a period mostly after
the transcript or memo was released, but there

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.270
was one polling day in there that was before
it was released.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.700
Some people may just not have seen the news
about that yet.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.350
Uh, but the trend is very clear.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:20.790
If they don't like the facts, they pretend
they don't exist and this makes it difficult

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.730
or even impossible to advance serious conversations
about what has to be done.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.230
It's similar with climate change where there
are real serious conversations about what

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:36.560
policies should we have, what degree of government
involvement should there be in a climate change?

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.560
And dealing with that.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.240
What about personal responsibility when dealing
with climate change?

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.450
Whatever question you want to talk about,
we can't even get on the same page about what

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:48.710
the facts are because some large portion of
the American right wing just refuses to accept

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.190
the facts on climate change.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:55.330
We can't possibly fix anything or even discuss
it in good faith.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:03:01.560
If one side doesn't accept the facts, and
sadly this is how I end up back at, we need

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.140
to get around them to win.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.150
We don't, we can't try to win with them.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.960
A conversation about how to proceed with Trump
or about the economy or about who to vote

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.080
for in 2020 or about tariffs.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.860
These conversations are pointless as ways
to engage with people about making change

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:22.420
in 2020 if they won't even accept basic facts,
including ones that their dear leader gives

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.420
them.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:27.270
The short answer is you can't and you shouldn't,
and we don't need to as the upside.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.760
I don't want to be a broken record again,
but half the country doesn't vote.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:36.240
Meaning you don't have to go out and find
people and convince them that voting for Trump

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.950
is a bad idea.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.610
That's not necessary to win this.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:44.910
You just need to find people who are already
on our side and just explain to them the importance

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.910
of voting.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.000
And that is much easier to do.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.000
It's still not easy.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.010
I've met people who don't vote, and it's not
easy to convince them that they should be

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.630
voting, but it is easier than convincing someone
who won't even believe Trump.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.300
When Trump says, we talked about Joe Biden
on the Ukrainian president phone call.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.629
Uh, and I don't even think that we should
bother doing it.

